{{!< default}}
{{!-- The TFR rail, first on the page and pinned under the masthead as on the reader (Ian, 2026-09-23). --}}
{{> "faith-received/_tfr-rail"}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Lexicon | The Faith Received | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
<meta name="description" content="Every term in the library, as its authors define it." />
{{!-- Dark mode: sets html[data-sd-theme] before paint, as the Scripture pages, the decks and the author room do. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/scripture-view-boot.js"}}&amp;frv=b619c4b13b360add"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "css/faith-tool-skin.css"}}&amp;frv=ef55f0e23f01f5c5">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "css/faith-lexicon.css"}}&amp;frv=59ceb17ff207998b">
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/lexicon/: the Lexicon, in this site's shell. The hero is the theme's; the body and its script (faith-lexicon.js)
     read the library worker's v1/lexicon files. Styles: css/faith-lexicon.css (scoped under main.tfr-lexicon). --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>
<main class="tfr-tool tfr-lexicon"><div class="wrap">
  <header class="lx-hd" id="lx-hd">
    <p class="lx-eyebrow"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Lexicon</p>
    <h1>Lexicon</h1>
    <p class="lx-sub">Every term in the library, as its authors define it.</p>
  </header>
  <p class="sr" id="lx-live" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div id="lx-boot" hidden></div>
  <div id="lx-listview">
    <div class="lx-tools">
      <form class="lx-find" role="search" id="lx-find"><label class="sr" for="lx-q">Search the lexicon</label><input id="lx-q" type="search" placeholder="Search terms: grace, gratia, &chi;&#940;&rho;&iota;&sigmaf;" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="80" enterkeyhint="search"></form>
      <div class="lx-tabs" id="lx-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Alphabet"><button type="button" data-t="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button><button type="button" data-t="en" aria-pressed="false">English</button><button type="button" data-t="grc" aria-pressed="false">Greek</button><button type="button" data-t="he" aria-pressed="false">Hebrew</button></div>
      <p class="lx-count"><span id="lx-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></p>
    </div>
    <nav class="lx-bar" id="lx-bar" aria-label="Jump to a letter"></nav>
    <div id="lx-all"></div>
    <div id="lx-found" hidden><div id="lx-found-cols"></div></div>
    <p class="lx-empty" id="lx-empty" hidden></p>
  </div>
  <article class="lx-entry" id="lx-entry" hidden></article>
  {{#> tfr-method}}<p>Terms, senses and the pages that define them were gathered by machine from the library&rsquo;s texts. A quote is the sentence on that page where the term or one of its forms appears. Where none does, the first lines of the page are shown. English lines of some works are machine translations.</p>{{/tfr-method}}
</div></main>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-lexicon.js"}}&amp;frv=c63e564da2abc089"></script>
